  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Clarifying Deployment Workflow**\n\nI\'m focusing on clarifying deployment procedures, specifically regarding the build process. I\'m noting that the project should build using `npm run`, as outlined in the guidelines. This is a key step I want to be certain I understand thoroughly for a smooth rollout, and I\'m documenting it for future reference.\n\n\n**Defining Core Features**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining the core features of this brief generator. I\'ve begun parsing the prompt requirements, breaking them down into essential elements. The core features seem to revolve around research input, which is key to generating the brief. I\'m noting the required and optional inputs, like topic, question, academic level, length, and preferred source.\n\n\n**Outlining Source Discovery**\n\nI\'m now outlining the source discovery module. I\'m focusing on integrating a search functionality that leverages Gemini 3.8 Flash with server-side search grounding. This should allow for multi-query web search retrieval and cross-checking, enabling the retrieval of live web sources, including their type, publisher, URL, and publication date, as well as de-duplication of results.\n\n\n**Detailing Brief Structure**\n\nI\'m now detailing the structure of the academic briefs I intend to generate. I\'ve broken down each section, from title and research question to the conclusion and references, along with formal language considerations. I\'m focusing on evidence-backed analysis with inline citations and the importance of including limitations and conflicting information. I\'m also including claims with identifiers and sources to verify the evidence.\n\n\n**Assessing Claim Validity**\n\nI\'m now establishing the criteria for claim verification, focusing on four states: Supported, Partially Supported, Contradicted, and Unverified. I\'m noting the need to explain the rationale for each verification status and include a direct link to the original source. I\'m also planning a filter by verification status and a disclaimer about the AI\'s limitations. Additionally, I\'m thinking about a results dashboard with research summary stats.\n\n\n**Visualizing Interactive Features**\n\nI\'m now visualizing the interactive features within the results dashboard to improve the user\'s research experience. I\'m imagining interactive evidence tables with claim IDs, sources, and verification status with an interactive \"inspect\" action. The source cards will include a credibility indicator. I\'m also planning inline citations to link claims and sources. Export options for markdown and PDF formats, and a \"Start New Research\" button, are essential. I\'m further outlining a prompt engineering workflow with eight distinct stages.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_89368"
