  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Design Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the styling and design prerequisites, specifically the color scheme. I\'ve taken note of the specified palette \342\200\223 navy, white, and restrained violet. I\'m exploring deep navy shades for headers, branding, and text, considering options like `#0A192F`, `#0F172A`, `#1E293B`, and `#334155` for their respective suitability. The next step is evaluating the white and violet components of the palette.\n\n\n**Refining Color and Typography**\n\nI\'ve finalized the color palette, incorporating violet accents like `#6366F1` and `#7C3AED`, while preserving a crisp white background with `#FFFFFF` or a soft slate. For borders, I\'m leaning towards `#E2E8F0`. Typography will embrace Newsreader for headings, Inter for UI elements, and JetBrains Mono for citations. I am now exploring design considerations, like zero-pill discipline. I am considering appropriate separators like \"\302\267\", \"/\", segmented controls for tabs.\n\n**Architecting Data Structures**\n\nNow, I\'m defining data structures. I\'ve formulated strongly-typed structures for academic levels, brief lengths, source types, and verification status. I\'ve also outlined a `SourceItem` structure including `id`, `title`, `url`, and `publisher` properties, all with appropriate types.\n\n\n**Defining Claim Attributes**\n\nI\'m now detailing crucial attributes for claim verification. I\'ve established types for `publishedDate`, `sourceType`, and credibility metrics (`score`, `tier`, `notes`). I\'ve also added `excerpt`, `accessible`, and `domain` properties for enhanced data representation. For `ClaimVerification`, I\'ve structured fields like `id`, `claimText`, `sourceIds`, `status`, `confidenceScore`, `rationale`, and `sectionRef`. I\'ve included optional `contradictionFlag` and `revisedText`.\n\n\n**Structuring Report Properties**\n\nI\'m presently focused on structuring the final report object. I\'ve defined key properties like `topic`, `researchQuestion`, and `academicLevel`. I\'m also including `generatedAt`, `executiveSummary`, `introduction`, `keyFindings` (as an array), and detailed sections for `evidenceAnalysis` (with citation markers), `limitationsAndConflictingInfo`, and `conclusion`. There will be a `references` array, as well as `claims` and `sources`, and a `metrics` object. I have specified the fields in all data structures within the new report format.\n\n\n**Mapping Workflow Stages**\n\nI\'m now mapping out an 8-stage prompt engineering workflow. I am defining each stage\'s title, description, and possible statuses (\'completed\', \'in_progress\', \'pending\'), with duration measured in milliseconds. I\'m focusing on how the backend will implement this structure, particularly with `@google/genai` and `gemini-3.8-flash`.\n\n\n**Implementing Search Capabilities**\n\nI\'m now integrating the search API. I\'m focusing on how `googleSearch` in Gemini 3.8 Flash can retrieve real-time data, and how it will return grounding metadata. I\'m prioritizing extracting real URLs, titles and search queries for the citation process. I\'m currently figuring out how to structure the multi-step verification process to ensure high-quality citations, including filtering and classifying sources.\n\n\n**Defining Verification Flow**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a new verification prompt that takes exact claims and excerpts and assigns a `supported`, `partially_supported`, `contradicted`, or `unverified` status, along with an epistemic rationale. I am considering incorporating an adversarial approach to this validation, and how to represent this data within the report, particularly how contradictory claims and unsupported claims are handled.\n\n\n"
