  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing Backend Logic**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `server.ts` file to build the backend generator. Key considerations are emerging: rigorous validations are essential. Specifically, ensuring the topic is required and at least three characters long. Also, user inputs need careful sanitization, treated as data, not instructions for the AI, for robust security.\n\n\n**Analyzing Prompt Engineering**\n\nI\'m now deep in an 8-stage prompt engineering workflow. Stage 1 focuses on interpreting the research topic and crafting the research question. I\'m formulating clear research scope and sub-questions based on academic level and preferred source types. Stage 2 involves source discovery using a Google Search integration, invoking Gemini 3.8 Flash to query authoritative topics. This process aims to get grounding metadata with web URIs and titles, then construct source cards from the results.\n\n\n**Evaluating Source Credibility**\n\nI\'m now focusing on assessing the reliability of sources, prioritizing domain authority (.gov, .edu, .org, journals), publication year, and organizational reputation. This leads to assigning credibility scores and tiers. Stage 4 involves extracting evidence (facts, figures, quotes) from sources, while Stage 5 drafts an academic brief with inline citations. Stage 6 rigorously evaluates factual claims against supporting evidence, assigning a status and confidence score to each.\n\n\n**Refining Verification & Presentation**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on Stages 7 and 8. Specifically, I\'m ensuring unsupported claims are revised or flagged with epistemic precision. I\'m also preparing to generate the final report with accurate APA citations, full URLs, and audit logs. Furthermore, I\'m considering a rich set of exemplar briefs for instant demonstration and testing, and support for Server-Sent Events (SSE) streaming. This way, the front-end can display the live progression through all 8 stages.\n\n\n"
