  code_action {
    action_spec {
      create_file {
        instruction: "# Verified Academic Brief Generator\n\nAn AI-powered academic research engine and epistemic verification dashboard built with React, Node.js, Tailwind CSS, and the Gemini API (using `gemini-3.8-flash` with Google Search Grounding).\n\nDeveloped for college AI Tools and Prompt Engineering coursework, this system accepts any research inquiry, retrieves authoritative online sources (.gov, .edu, peer-reviewed journals, official reports, reputable news), synthesizes a structured academic brief with inline citations, and adversarially verifies every major factual assertion against verbatim retrieved source excerpts.\n\n---\n\n## Key Features\n\n1. **Deterministic 8-Stage Prompt Engineering Architecture**:\n   - **Stage 1: Topic Interpretation & Question Formulation** \342\200\223 Scopes academic breadth, refines research questions, and establishes inquiry criteria.\n   - **Stage 2: Multi-Source Discovery via Search Grounding** \342\200\223 Interrogates live web search grounding indices to discover real, authoritative documents.\n   - **Stage 3: Credibility, Freshness & Authority Evaluation** \342\200\223 Deduplicates URLs, scores domain authority (.gov, .edu, .org, recognized journals), and checks metadata completeness.\n   - **Stage 4: Evidence Extraction** \342\200\223 Isolates verbatim empirical excerpts, statistical parameters, and direct factual propositions.\n   - **Stage 5: Structured Academic Brief Drafting** \342\200\223 Composes 6 structured academic sections with inline citation tags (`[S1]`, `[S2]`).\n   - **Stage 6: Claim-Level Evidence Verification** \342\200\223 Adversarially audits every major factual claim against its supporting source excerpt, assigning statuses:\n     - `Supported`: Excerpt directly confirms the assertion with matching numbers and scope.\n     - `Partially Supported`: Excerpt provides directional evidence but lacks specific metrics.\n     - `Contradicted`: Excerpt or empirical reality refutes the claim.\n     - `Unverified`: Excerpt is missing, vague, or inconclusive.\n   - **Stage 7: Revision & Nuance** \342\200\223 Rewrites overreaching assertions, applies epistemic hedging, and flags contradictions in the Limitations section.\n   - **Stage 8: Reference Ledger Compilation** \342\200\223 Formats complete APA/IEEE bibliographic entries with persistent hyperlinks.\n\n2. **Claim-Level Evidence Ledger**:\n   - Unique claim identifiers (`CLM-001`, `CLM-002`, etc.).\n   - Side-by-side comparison between the audited proposition and the verbatim source excerpt.\n   - Real-time epistemic rationale explaining the verification rating.\n   - Epistemic revision highlights for contradicted or unverified statements.\n   - Direct clickable inspection of the original source URL.\n\n3. **Academic Dashboard & Reader**:\n   - Clean academic design with a navy, white, and restrained violet palette.\n   - Editorial typography: Newsreader serif for scholarly text, Inter for interface elements, JetBrains Mono for citation keys and timestamps.\n   - Full Export options: Copy formatted Markdown, Download `.md` document, and clean Print / PDF preview.\n   - Instant Demo Pre-sets for fast evaluation:\n     - *mRNA Vaccine Distribution Equity in LMICs*\n     - *Post-Quantum Cryptography & NIST Standards*\n     - *CRISPR-Cas9 Human Germline Editing Ethics*\n     - *Direct Air Carbon Capture Efficacy*\n\n---\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 index.html                   # HTML entry point with Newsreader, Inter & JetBrains Mono fonts\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 metadata.json                # AI Studio application metadata\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 package.json                 # Dependencies & full-stack scripts (tsx server.ts)\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 server.ts                    # Express server with Vite middleware, REST & SSE streaming\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 server/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 geminiWorkflow.ts        # 8-Stage Prompt Engineering & Gemini Search Grounding engine\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 sampleData.ts            # Curated academic briefs with complete verification ledgers\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 App.tsx                  # Root app coordinating pipeline, tabs, and modals\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 index.css                # Tailwind CSS v4 styling, font mappings, and print styles\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 main.tsx                 # React DOM mount point\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 types/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 index.ts             # Strongly-typed models for briefs, claims, sources, and stages\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 components/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Header.tsx           # Application header with sample selector & reset\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ResearchForm.tsx     # Topic input, academic level, length, and source filters\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 StageProgressTracker.tsx # 8-stage stepper with live progress animation\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 MetricsBar.tsx       # Verification rigor score, source counts, and claim breakdown\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 BriefViewer.tsx      # Formal scholarly brief with interactive inline citations\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ClaimsTable.tsx      # Evidence verification table with filterable statuses\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 SourcesList.tsx      # Discovered source cards with authority scores and excerpts\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 StageAuditView.tsx   # Detailed telemetry for all 8 prompt engineering stages\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ReferencesView.tsx   # APA/IEEE formatted citations with copy and URL actions\n\342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 SourceDetailModal.tsx # Inspect source telemetry, excerpt, and linked claims\n```\n\n---\n\n## Environment Variables\n\nCopy `.env.example` to `.env`:\n\n```bash\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini API calls and search grounding.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"your-gemini-api-key-here\"\n\n# PORT: Server port (defaults to 3000)\nPORT=3000\n```\n\n---\n\n## Local Setup & Development\n\n1. **Install dependencies**:\n   ```bash\n   npm install\n   ```\n\n2. **Run Development Server**:\n   ```bash\n   npm run dev\n   ```\n   The dev server will start on `http://localhost:3000`, serving both the backend API and the Vite React frontend.\n\n3. **Build for Production**:\n   ```bash\n   npm run build\n   ```\n\n4. **Run Production Server**:\n   ```bash\n   npm run start\n   ```\n\n---\n\n## Deployment Instructions\n\n### Vercel / Netlify\n1. Connect repository.\n2. Build command: `npm run build`\n3. Output directory: `dist`\n4. Set `GEMINI_API_KEY` in environment variables.\n5. For full-stack API routes, ensure serverless proxy or deploy the Express backend to a Node.js container (e.g., Render, Railway, or Google Cloud Run).\n\n### Google Cloud Run / Docker\n```dockerfile\nFROM node:22-alpine\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY package*.json ./\nRUN npm install\nCOPY . .\nRUN npm run build\nEXPOSE 3000\nCMD [\"npm\", \"run\", \"start\"]\n```\n\n---\n\n## Academic Demonstration Walkthrough\n\n1. Open the application at `http://localhost:3000`.\n2. Click **\"mRNA Equity\"** or **\"Post-Quantum NIST\"** in the top bar or preset buttons to instantly inspect a pre-verified brief.\n3. Observe the **Metrics Bar**:\n   - Total Vetted Sources (e.g. 5 / 14 discovered)\n   - Audited Claims (e.g. 6 claims evaluated)\n   - Supported vs. Contradicted claims breakdown\n   - Epistemic Rigor Score (e.g. 92/100)\n4. Click on the **Claim Verification Ledger** tab:\n   - Filter by **\"Contradicted\"** to observe claim `CLM-004`: Notice how the false proposition regarding patent-only immediate fixes was caught and revised to reflect technical bioreactor constraints.\n   - Click **\"Inspect\"** on any source row to review the verbatim retrieved excerpt.\n5. Click on the **8-Stage Pipeline Audit** tab to inspect each isolated stage\'s runtime, telemetry, and non-hallucination guardrails.\n6. Click **\"Copy Markdown\"** or **\"Print / PDF\"** to export the brief.\n7. Click **\"New Research\"** to submit a custom research topic!\n"
        path {
          absolute_uri: "file:///README.md"
        }
        overwrite: true
      }
    }
