  planner_response {
    response: "### Verified Academic Brief Generator\n\nThe **Verified Academic Brief Generator** is now built and operational. This web application accepts any research topic, investigates it using authoritative web sources, synthesizes a formal academic brief with inline citations, and adversarially audits every major factual claim against verbatim evidence excerpts.\n\n---\n\n### Core Architecture & Capabilities\n\n1. **Deterministic 8-Stage Prompt Engineering Architecture**:\n   - **Stage 1 (Topic Scoping & Research Question Formulation)**: Decomposes topics, establishes academic level guidelines (*Beginner*, *Undergraduate*, *Advanced*), and formulates targeted search vectors.\n   - **Stage 2 (Multi-Source Discovery via Search Grounding)**: Uses Gemini 3.8 Flash (`gemini-3.8-flash`) with Google Search Grounding to query real-time indexes across government repositories (`.gov`, WHO, UN), accredited universities (`.edu`), peer-reviewed journals (*Nature*, *Science*, *The Lancet*, *IEEE*), and official reports (*IMF*, *World Bank*, *IPCC*).\n   - **Stage 3 (Credibility, Freshness & Authority Evaluation)**: Canonicalizes and deduplicates URLs, classifies publisher domains, and calculates authority scores (0\342\200\223100) and credibility tiers.\n   - **Stage 4 (Verbatim Evidence Extraction)**: Isolates exact empirical excerpts, numerical figures, and factual findings from accessible content, explicitly flagging missing publication dates.\n   - **Stage 5 (Evidence-Backed Brief Drafting)**: Synthesizes a structured academic brief complete with inline citation anchors (`[S1]`, `[S2]`).\n   - **Stage 6 (Claim-Level Evidence Verification)**: The core epistemic audit engine assigns unique claim identifiers (`CLM-001`, `CLM-002`, ...), matches each claim with cited source excerpts, and rigorously grades evidence concordance into four distinct statuses:\n     - **Supported**: Verbatim excerpt confirms the factual assertion with matching figures and scope.\n     - **Partially Supported**: Excerpt provides directional evidence but lacks specific parameters.\n     - **Contradicted**: Empirical source contradicts or disproves the assertion.\n     - **Unverified**: Excerpt is missing, vague, or insufficient to prove the claim.\n   - **Stage 7 (Revision, Nuance & Contradiction Resolution)**: Flags contradicted or unsupported claims, applies epistemic hedging in the text, and updates the *Limitations & Conflicting Information* section.\n   - **Stage 8 (Reference Ledger Compilation)**: Generates APA/IEEE bibliographic entries with persistent hyperlinks and computes verification rigor metrics.\n\n2. **Claim-Level Evidence Ledger**:\n   - Filter claims by status: *All*, *Supported*, *Partially Supported*, *Contradicted*, or *Unverified*.\n   - Inspect side-by-side comparisons of the audited proposition, revised statement (if contradicted), supporting source, verbatim evidence excerpt, and epistemic audit rationale.\n   - Direct button to open the original source URL.\n\n3. **Academic Results Dashboard**:\n   - **Metrics Bar**: Verification Rigor Index (0\342\200\223100), total sources vetted vs. discovered, audited claims breakdown, and average source authority.\n   - **Interactive Citations**: Clickable `[S1]` and `[S2]` tags open an inspection modal displaying the source\'s publisher, publication date, credibility appraisal, excerpt, and all linked claims.\n   - **8-Stage Pipeline Audit**: Inspect duration in milliseconds, status, and output telemetry for every stage in the prompt pipeline.\n   - **Scholarly Export Tools**: One-click **Copy Markdown**, **Download `.md`**, and clean **Print / PDF preview** with academic print layout rules.\n\n4. **Curated Demonstration Topics & Fast Previews**:\n   - Includes instant verified dossiers on *Socioeconomic Implications of Global mRNA Vaccine Distribution Equity in LMICs* and *Post-Quantum Cryptography: NIST Standards & Migration Complexity*, demonstrating how contradicted claims (e.g., patent-only quick fixes or 500ms latency myths) are caught, flagged, and revised.\n\n---\n\n### Verification and Health\n\n- Dev server running on `http://0.0.0.0:3000` (`tsx server.ts`).\n- Server `/api/health` confirmed operational with `gemini-3.8-flash`.\n- TypeScript (`tsc --noEmit`) and Vite compilation succeeded with 0 errors."
    thinking: "**Verifying Requirements Checklist**\n\nI\'m checking the initial requirements checklist for the \"Verified Academic Brief Generator.\" I\'ve confirmed the project name consistency across different components. My current focus is on the stated objective: accepting a topic and researching it. I\'m thinking about the best approach for integrating research tools.\n\n\n**Defining Core Features**\n\nI am now focusing on the core features. I\'ve begun organizing them into several modules, like research input, source discovery, academic brief generation, and claim-level evidence verification. I\'m prioritizing source credibility and thinking about how to integrate Gemini\'s search grounding for efficient and trustworthy information retrieval.\n\n\n**Detailing Project Capabilities**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics. I\'m focusing on unique claim IDs and their connection to sources and evidence. A results dashboard is taking shape, and I\'m fleshing out features like the evidence table and reference sections. I\342\200\231m thinking about the user experience, zero-pill discipline, the 8-stage progress tracker, and a restrained palette. The plan for an 8-stage prompt engineering workflow is coming together. Security aspects are under consideration.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### Verified Academic Brief Generator\n\nThe **Verified Academic Brief Generator** is now built and operational. This web application accepts any research topic, investigates it using authoritative web sources, synthesizes a formal academic brief with inline citations, and adversarially audits every major factual claim against verbatim evidence excerpts.\n\n---\n\n### Core Architecture & Capabilities\n\n1. **Deterministic 8-Stage Prompt Engineering Architecture**:\n   - **Stage 1 (Topic Scoping & Research Question Formulation)**: Decomposes topics, establishes academic level guidelines (*Beginner*, *Undergraduate*, *Advanced*), and formulates targeted search vectors.\n   - **Stage 2 (Multi-Source Discovery via Search Grounding)**: Uses Gemini 3.8 Flash (`gemini-3.8-flash`) with Google Search Grounding to query real-time indexes across government repositories (`.gov`, WHO, UN), accredited universities (`.edu`), peer-reviewed journals (*Nature*, *Science*, *The Lancet*, *IEEE*), and official reports (*IMF*, *World Bank*, *IPCC*).\n   - **Stage 3 (Credibility, Freshness & Authority Evaluation)**: Canonicalizes and deduplicates URLs, classifies publisher domains, and calculates authority scores (0\342\200\223100) and credibility tiers.\n   - **Stage 4 (Verbatim Evidence Extraction)**: Isolates exact empirical excerpts, numerical figures, and factual findings from accessible content, explicitly flagging missing publication dates.\n   - **Stage 5 (Evidence-Backed Brief Drafting)**: Synthesizes a structured academic brief complete with inline citation anchors (`[S1]`, `[S2]`).\n   - **Stage 6 (Claim-Level Evidence Verification)**: The core epistemic audit engine assigns unique claim identifiers (`CLM-001`, `CLM-002`, ...), matches each claim with cited source excerpts, and rigorously grades evidence concordance into four distinct statuses:\n     - **Supported**: Verbatim excerpt confirms the factual assertion with matching figures and scope.\n     - **Partially Supported**: Excerpt provides directional evidence but lacks specific parameters.\n     - **Contradicted**: Empirical source contradicts or disproves the assertion.\n     - **Unverified**: Excerpt is missing, vague, or insufficient to prove the claim.\n   - **Stage 7 (Revision, Nuance & Contradiction Resolution)**: Flags contradicted or unsupported claims, applies epistemic hedging in the text, and updates the *Limitations & Conflicting Information* section.\n   - **Stage 8 (Reference Ledger Compilation)**: Generates APA/IEEE bibliographic entries with persistent hyperlinks and computes verification rigor metrics.\n\n2. **Claim-Level Evidence Ledger**:\n   - Filter claims by status: *All*, *Supported*, *Partially Supported*, *Contradicted*, or *Unverified*.\n   - Inspect side-by-side comparisons of the audited proposition, revised statement (if contradicted), supporting source, verbatim evidence excerpt, and epistemic audit rationale.\n   - Direct button to open the original source URL.\n\n3. **Academic Results Dashboard**:\n   - **Metrics Bar**: Verification Rigor Index (0\342\200\223100), total sources vetted vs. discovered, audited claims breakdown, and average source authority.\n   - **Interactive Citations**: Clickable `[S1]` and `[S2]` tags open an inspection modal displaying the source\'s publisher, publication date, credibility appraisal, excerpt, and all linked claims.\n   - **8-Stage Pipeline Audit**: Inspect duration in milliseconds, status, and output telemetry for every stage in the prompt pipeline.\n   - **Scholarly Export Tools**: One-click **Copy Markdown**, **Download `.md`**, and clean **Print / PDF preview** with academic print layout rules.\n\n4. **Curated Demonstration Topics & Fast Previews**:\n   - Includes instant verified dossiers on *Socioeconomic Implications of Global mRNA Vaccine Distribution Equity in LMICs* and *Post-Quantum Cryptography: NIST Standards & Migration Complexity*, demonstrating how contradicted claims (e.g., patent-only quick fixes or 500ms latency myths) are caught, flagged, and revised.\n\n---\n\n### Verification and Health\n\n- Dev server running on `http://0.0.0.0:3000` (`tsx server.ts`).\n- Server `/api/health` confirmed operational with `gemini-3.8-flash`.\n- TypeScript (`tsc --noEmit`) and Vite compilation succeeded with 0 errors."
